    {
      "id": "p0110-b005",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "source": {
        "text": "In 2017, 8-4 announced details about Underta/e's upcoming Japanese release. This announcement included a video of Sans using oira. Fans accustomed to the fan-made translations reacted loudly to this unexpected pronoun choice - some responded with intense negativity, some responded with bewilderment, and others responded with humor. Online reactions grew so intense that the incident was quickly dubbed the \"Oira Shock\".",
        "raw": "In 2017, 8-4 announced details about Underta/e's upcoming Japanese release.\nThis announcement included a video of Sans using oira. Fans accustomed to\nthe fan-made translations reacted loudly to this unexpected pronoun choice -\nsome responded with intense negativity, some responded with bewilderment,\nand others responded with humor. Online reactions grew so intense that the\nincident was quickly dubbed the \"Oira Shock\".",
        "status": "corrected",
        "languages": [
          "en"
        ],
        "bbox": [
          0.29876016,
          0.40715714,
          0.89458333,
          0.51122857
        ],
        "mask_bbox": [
          0.2949187,
          0.40644286,
          0.90072154,
          0.5123
        ],
        "line_ids": [
          16,
          17,
          18,
          19,
          20,
          21
        ]
      },
      "translation": {
        "text": "2017年，8-4 公布了 Undertale 即将推出日语版的详情，其中有一段 Sans 使用 oira 的视频。习惯了粉丝译版的玩家对这个出人意料的自称反应强烈：有人激烈反对，有人困惑，也有人拿它开玩笑。网上反响越来越大，这件事很快被称为“Oira Shock”（Oira 冲击）。",
        "status": "draft",
        "spans": [
