    {
      "id": "p0110-b010",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "source": {
        "text": "Sans' use of oira in the final Japanese release actually came as two simultaneous shocks. First, it indicated that Toby had indeed given oira his stamp of approval. Second, it conflicted with Toby's statement from years earlier that Sans seemed like the type of character to use the pronoun boku. As a result of all of this, Sans' pronoun was - and still is - a serious and unique issue among Japanese fans.",
        "raw": "Sans' use of oira in the final Japanese release actually came as two\nsimultaneous shocks. First, it indicated that Toby had indeed given oira his\nstamp of approval. Second, it conflicted with Toby's statement from years\nearlier that Sans seemed like the type of character to use the pronoun boku. As\na result of all of this, Sans' pronoun was - and still is - a serious and unique\nissue among Japanese fans.",
        "status": "corrected",
        "languages": [
          "en"
        ],
        "bbox": [
          0.30145325,
          0.70865714,
          0.89868902,
          0.81240714
        ],
        "mask_bbox": [
          0.2949187,
          0.70794286,
          0.90072154,
          0.81347857
        ],
        "line_ids": [
          30,
          31,
          32,
          33,
          34,
          35
        ]
      },
      "translation": {
        "text": "Sans 在最终日语版中使用 oira，其实同时带来了两重冲击。首先，这表明 Toby 确实认可了 oira。其次，这与 Toby 几年前的说法相矛盾：他当时觉得 Sans 像是会用 boku（我）自称的角色。因此，Sans 的自称在日本粉丝中成了一个严肃而独特的话题，直到现在仍是如此。",
        "status": "draft",
